			}
		}
					
	IOC vs DI

	IoC
	→ Principle / design principle
	→ Control of object creation and management is transferred
	  from application code to Spring.

	DI
	→ Technique/design pattern used to implement IoC
	→ Spring provides required dependencies to a class.

	Spring IoC Container
	→ Container responsible for creating and managing Spring Beans.
	→ ApplicationContext is a commonly used Spring IoC container interface.

	Traditional Spring:
	→ Create beans.xml
	→ Define beans using <bean>
	→ Load using:

	ApplicationContext context =
		new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("beans.xml");

	Spring Boot:
	→ No need to normally create beans.xml
	→ Start application using:

	SpringApplication.run(Application.class, args);

	→ Spring creates ApplicationContext
	→ Component scanning finds @Component, @Service,
	  @Repository, @Controller, etc.
	→ Spring creates and manages those objects as Beans
	→ Spring performs Dependency Injection.
			
